  "step_2": "The individual considered the monetary outcomes and their probabilities. They explicitly mention that 'die 5 Euro kommt es nicht an' (the 5 Euros doesn't matter). This indicates that the individual disregarded the -5 Euros in Lottery A as insignificant. The justification focuses on the negligible impact of the small loss in Lottery A, implying that the decision was driven by the perception that the small loss is irrelevant. The individual did not mention probability distributions, skewness, or the relative weight of unfavorable outcomes. There is no reference to the structure of the probability mass or the shape of the distribution. The deliberation centers on the perceived insignificance of the small loss, not on the skewness of the lotteries.",
